; NSIS additions to electron-builder's installer for the coop window package
; (master plan D1d, F3). Included through nsis.include in electron-builder.cjs.
;
; F3 (Aaron 2026-10-20): coop installs once per machine. The installer is
; per-machine (nsis.perMachine), so Windows asks for an administrator once and
; every account shares the program; each account keeps its own data under its
; user folder (%USERPROFILE%\.coop). The pieces NSIS does not do itself live in
; the snapshot's PowerShell scripts, run with the built-in Windows PowerShell:
;
;   customInit        before anything is written: this account's older
;                     per-user coop (HKCU InstallLocation, else the folder of
;                     its UninstallString, else %LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs\coop) is
;                     uninstalled completely (not --updated), so its own
;                     uninstaller also drops the `coop` link and "coop"
;                     shortcuts its first launch wrote; the machine shim then
;                     serves the account. ~\.coop is never touched.
;   customInstall     scripts\machine-install.ps1: the machine shim
;                     <app>\bin\coop.cmd on the machine PATH (the `coop`
;                     command for every account), the machine marker, the
;                     "coop update" scheduled task (scripts\auto-update.ps1 as
;                     SYSTEM installs each new release silently), the shared
;                     standards folder, and the removal of EVERY account's
;                     older per-user package, link and icons (elevated, so
;                     the other accounts' copies go too; their ~\.coop stays).
;   customUnInstall   before the uninstaller deletes the package, so the
;                     snapshot's scripts are still there: window-uninstall.ps1
;                     removes the `coop` launcher link and "coop" shortcuts an
;                     older package's first launch wrote, only when they point
;                     into this install dir; machine-install.ps1 -Remove undoes
;                     the shim, the PATH entry, the marker and the task.
;                     window-uninstall.ps1 also removes the "coop at sign-in"
;                     Run value (coop startup) of this account and of every
;                     signed-in account, only when it starts this install's
;                     scripts\sign-in.ps1.
;                     Best-effort: the scripts never fail the uninstall. An
;                     upgrade (the new installer runs this uninstaller with
;                     --updated) keeps everything: the new version installs
;                     into the same folder and re-runs the machine step (D1k).
;   customRemoveFiles the uninstaller's removal of the program files. On an
;                     upgrade coop.exe (with Electron's own files and
;                     resources\app.asar, so it starts and says "coop is
;                     updating") and the marked runtime packs stay in place
;                     while everything else goes and the new version is copied in:
;                     a taskbar pin whose target is missing when Explorer
;                     starts is dropped by Windows for good (a client VM,
;                     2026-11-09: a sign-in during the overnight update lost
;                     the pin). The new coop.exe overwrites it at the end. A
;                     real uninstall removes the folder whole, as before.
;                     scripts/auto-update.ps1 and a bootstrap over an installed
;                     window run the installer with --updated, so the previous
;                     uninstaller also keeps the all-users "coop" shortcuts
;                     and their pins (electron-builder's --keep-shortcuts).
;   customInstall (packs) before the machine step: each folder of
;                     resources\runtime (Node, Pi, the extensions, Git, Python,
;                     the wheels, the Azure CLI, the ODBC installers) ships as
;                     its own 7z, not in electron-builder's app archive (which
;                     is unpacked into %TEMP% and copied file by file). coopPack
;                     unpacks a pack straight into its folder, and only when the
;                     folder's .coop-pack marker does not name this build's
;                     content id (packs.nsh, generated by build-installer.mjs).
;                     customRemoveFiles keeps marked folders on an upgrade, so a
;                     release that changed none of them rewrites a few hundred
;                     files instead of ~34,000 (a client VM's update took 19
;                     minutes, 2026-11-11). Folders that are no longer packs go.
;   customCheckAppRunning   electron-builder's own "is coop running" check,
;                     with the installer's step lines around it (below).
;   customWelcomePage / customFinishPage   what the installer says.
;
; What the installer says while it works (Aaron 2026-10-29: the install takes
; minutes and showed only a bar). electron-builder's install section starts
; with SetDetailsPrint none, so on its own the page names no step at all.
; coopStep shows a step on the status line above the bar, then sends
; electron-builder's own lines to the details list only (never shown:
; ShowInstDetails nevershow), so the step stays readable; step 3 shows each of
; machine-install.ps1's lines (nsExec::ExecToLog) on the status line instead:
;   Step 1 of 3  closing coop if it is open (customCheckAppRunning)
;   Step 2 of 3  the previous version's files out, this version's in: the
;                longest step (electron-builder's uninstallOldVersion and
;                installApplicationFiles; no hook between them)
;   Step 3 of 3  machine-install.ps1 (customInstall), each of its lines shown
;
; ${APP_GUID} is electron-builder's uninstall key for this appId (the same in
; every mode); $installMode is "all" for a per-machine install (multiUser.nsh).
;
; The installer is a 32-bit process: "$SYSDIR\WindowsPowerShell" is the 32-bit
; PowerShell under file-system redirection. coopPowerShell picks the 64-bit one
; through Sysnative on a 64-bit Windows (schtasks and the per-account sweep run
; there), else the only one. machine-install.ps1 logs every step to
; %ProgramData%\coop\logs\machine-install.log; the message box names it, and
; a failed machine step makes the installer exit 3 (silent runs included).

!include x64.nsh
!include FileFunc.nsh
!include WordFunc.nsh

!macro coopPowerShell OUT
  StrCpy ${OUT} "$SYSDIR\WindowsPowerShell\v1.0\powershell.exe"
  ${if} ${RunningX64}
    StrCpy ${OUT} "$WINDIR\Sysnative\WindowsPowerShell\v1.0\powershell.exe"
  ${endIf}
!macroend

; With customCheckAppRunning defined, allowOnlyOneInstallerInstance.nsh no
; longer includes what its _CHECK_APP_RUNNING needs (GetProcessInfo and the
; pid variable), so they are included here (the include dir is electron-builder's).
!ifndef GetProcessInfo
  !include "getProcessInfo.nsh"
!endif
Var pid

!macro coopStep TEXT
  SetDetailsPrint both
  DetailPrint "${TEXT}"
  SetDetailsPrint listonly
!macroend

; The runtime packs (see the header): build-installer.mjs writes packs.nsh
; beside this file (electron-builder's include dir) before every build, and a
; build without it stops here rather than ship an installer with no runtime.
!include "packs.nsh"

!ifndef BUILD_UNINSTALLER
  Var coopPackFailed
!endif

; One pack: keep the folder when its marker names ID and its CHECK file is
; there, else replace it from the embedded 7z (stored as is: it is already
; compressed). The marker is written last, so a cut-off unpack is redone.
!macro coopPack DIR ID FILES CHECK FILE
  StrCpy $R6 ""
  ${if} ${FileExists} "$INSTDIR\resources\runtime\${DIR}\.coop-pack"
  ${andIf} ${FileExists} "$INSTDIR\resources\runtime\${DIR}\${CHECK}"
    ClearErrors
    FileOpen $R5 "$INSTDIR\resources\runtime\${DIR}\.coop-pack" r
    ${ifNot} ${Errors}
      FileRead $R5 $R6
      FileClose $R5
    ${endIf}
  ${endIf}
  ${if} $R6 == "${ID}"
    !insertmacro coopStep "Step 2 of 3: ${DIR} is unchanged, kept as it is"
  ${else}
    !insertmacro coopStep "Step 2 of 3: unpacking ${DIR} (${FILES} files)"
    RMDir /r "$INSTDIR\resources\runtime\${DIR}"
    CreateDirectory "$INSTDIR\resources\runtime\${DIR}"
    SetOutPath "$INSTDIR\resources\runtime\${DIR}"
    !ifdef COMPRESS
      SetCompress off
    !endif
    File "/oname=$PLUGINSDIR\coop-pack.7z" "${FILE}"
    !ifdef COMPRESS
      SetCompress "${COMPRESS}"
    !endif
    Nsis7z::Extract "$PLUGINSDIR\coop-pack.7z"
    Delete "$PLUGINSDIR\coop-pack.7z"
    SetOutPath $INSTDIR
    ${if} ${FileExists} "$INSTDIR\resources\runtime\${DIR}\${CHECK}"
      FileOpen $R5 "$INSTDIR\resources\runtime\${DIR}\.coop-pack" w
      FileWrite $R5 "${ID}"
      FileClose $R5
    ${else}
      DetailPrint "could not unpack ${DIR}: ${CHECK} is missing"
      StrCpy $coopPackFailed "yes"
    ${endIf}
  ${endIf}
!macroend

; Folders of resources\runtime that are not this build's packs (an older
; layout, or a pack a later release dropped) go.
!macro coopPruneRuntime
  FindFirst $R7 $R8 "$INSTDIR\resources\runtime\*"
  ${DoWhile} $R8 != ""
    ${if} $R8 != "."
    ${andIf} $R8 != ".."
    ${andIf} ${FileExists} "$INSTDIR\resources\runtime\$R8\*.*"
      !insertmacro coopIsPack $R8 $R6
      ${if} $R6 == "no"
        DetailPrint "removing resources\runtime\$R8 (not part of this version)"
        RMDir /r "$INSTDIR\resources\runtime\$R8"
      ${endIf}
    ${endIf}
    FindNext $R7 $R8
  ${Loop}
  FindClose $R7
!macroend

!macro customCheckAppRunning
  !ifndef BUILD_UNINSTALLER
    !insertmacro coopStep "Step 1 of 3: checking that coop is not running"
  !endif
  !insertmacro IS_POWERSHELL_AVAILABLE
  !insertmacro _CHECK_APP_RUNNING
  !ifndef BUILD_UNINSTALLER
    ${if} ${FileExists} "$INSTDIR\Uninstall coop.exe"
      !insertmacro coopStep "Step 2 of 3: replacing coop's program files with this version's (the longest step: several minutes)"
    ${else}
      !insertmacro coopStep "Step 2 of 3: copying coop's program files: the window, Node.js, Pi, Python, Git, the Azure CLI (the longest step: several minutes)"
    ${endIf}
  !endif
!macroend

!macro customWelcomePage
  !define MUI_WELCOMEPAGE_TITLE "coop"
  !define MUI_WELCOMEPAGE_TEXT "coop installs once for every account on this computer.$\r$\n$\r$\nEach Windows account keeps its own client's sessions, memory and backups under its user folder.$\r$\n$\r$\nUpdates install themselves overnight.$\r$\n$\r$\nInstalling takes several minutes, and the first time each account opens coop it sets up that account's tools for a few more; a window shows each step.$\r$\n$\r$\nClick Next to continue."
  !insertmacro MUI_PAGE_WELCOME
!macroend

!macro customFinishPage
  !define MUI_FINISHPAGE_TITLE "coop is installed"
  !define MUI_FINISHPAGE_TEXT "coop is installed for every account on this computer: open coop from the Start Menu or the Desktop, or type coop in a new terminal.$\r$\n$\r$\nUpdates install themselves overnight; nothing to run by hand."
  !insertmacro MUI_PAGE_FINISH
!macroend

!macro customInit
  ${if} $installMode == "all"
    ReadRegStr $R2 HKCU "Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Uninstall\${APP_GUID}" "InstallLocation"
    ${if} $R2 == ""
      ReadRegStr $R2 HKCU "Software\${APP_GUID}" "InstallLocation"
    ${endIf}
    ${if} $R2 == ""
      ; A v0.37.0 per-user install wrote no InstallLocation: take the folder
      ; from its uninstall command, "<dir>\Uninstall coop.exe" /currentuser.
      ReadRegStr $R3 HKCU "Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Uninstall\${APP_GUID}" "UninstallString"
      ${if} $R3 != ""
        StrCpy $R4 $R3 1
        ${if} $R4 == '"'
          StrCpy $R3 $R3 "" 1
          ${WordFind} $R3 '"' "+1" $R3
        ${endIf}
        ${GetParent} $R3 $R2
      ${endIf}
    ${endIf}
    ${if} $R2 == ""
    ${andIf} ${FileExists} "$LOCALAPPDATA\Programs\coop\Uninstall coop.exe"
      StrCpy $R2 "$LOCALAPPDATA\Programs\coop"
    ${endIf}
    ; Only a local folder: an uninstaller on a network path is never run elevated.
    StrCpy $R5 $R2 2
    ${if} $R5 == "\\"
      DetailPrint "not running the older coop's uninstaller from the network path $R2"
      StrCpy $R2 ""
    ${endIf}
    ${if} $R2 != ""
    ${andIf} ${FileExists} "$R2\Uninstall coop.exe"
      DetailPrint "removing this account's older coop at $R2 (its data under the user folder stays)"
      ExecWait '"$R2\Uninstall coop.exe" /S /currentuser _?=$R2' $R0
      Delete "$R2\Uninstall coop.exe"
      RMDir "$R2"
      DeleteRegKey HKCU "Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Uninstall\${APP_GUID}"
      DeleteRegKey HKCU "Software\${APP_GUID}"
    ${endIf}
  ${endIf}
!macroend

!macro customInstall
  ; The folder, for the next installer and for coop doctor (v0.37.0 wrote none).
  WriteRegStr SHCTX "Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Uninstall\${APP_GUID}" "InstallLocation" "$INSTDIR"
  ; The runtime packs, before the machine step (it runs the ODBC installers from them).
  StrCpy $coopPackFailed ""
  !insertmacro coopUnpackRuntime
  !insertmacro coopPruneRuntime
  ${if} $installMode == "all"
    !insertmacro coopStep "Step 3 of 3: setting up coop for every account (the coop command, the SQL Server ODBC driver, the update task, older per-account copies)"
    SetDetailsPrint both
    !insertmacro coopPowerShell $R9
    nsExec::ExecToLog '"$R9" -NoLogo -NoProfile -NonInteractive -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File "$INSTDIR\resources\coop\scripts\machine-install.ps1" -InstallDir "$INSTDIR"'
    Pop $0
    ${if} $0 != 0
      DetailPrint "machine-install.ps1 exited $0 (log: %ProgramData%\coop\logs\machine-install.log)"
      ; The installer's own exit code says so too (3: the files are in, the
      ; machine setup did not finish), so a silent run from scripts\bootstrap.ps1
      ; or scripts\auto-update.ps1 reports the failure instead of success.
      SetErrorLevel 3
      ${ifNot} ${Silent}
        MessageBox MB_OK|MB_ICONEXCLAMATION "coop is installed, but the coop command for every account, its update task or the removal of older per-account copies did not finish (code $0).$\r$\n$\r$\nThe log: %ProgramData%\coop\logs\machine-install.log$\r$\n$\r$\nRun this as an administrator, then try again:$\r$\npowershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File $\"$INSTDIR\resources\coop\scripts\machine-install.ps1$\" -InstallDir $\"$INSTDIR$\""
      ${endIf}
    ${endIf}
  ${endIf}
  ${if} $coopPackFailed == "yes"
    ; 4: part of the runtime did not unpack (disk full, a file held open); the
    ; details list names the folder. The next install unpacks it again.
    SetErrorLevel 4
    ${ifNot} ${Silent}
      MessageBox MB_OK|MB_ICONEXCLAMATION "coop is installed, but part of its runtime did not unpack (the disk may be full). Run this installer again."
    ${endIf}
  ${endIf}
!macroend

; An upgrade's removal of resources\: everything but the runtime folders
; that carry a .coop-pack marker (the new installer keeps the ones whose
; content it would unpack again, coopPack, and replaces the rest).
!macro coopRemoveResources
  Push $R5
  Push $R6
  Push $R3
  Push $R4
  FindFirst $R5 $R6 "$INSTDIR\resources\*"
  ${DoWhile} $R6 != ""
    ${if} $R6 != "."
    ${andIf} $R6 != ".."
    ${andIf} $R6 != "app.asar"
      ${if} $R6 == "runtime"
        FindFirst $R3 $R4 "$INSTDIR\resources\runtime\*"
        ${DoWhile} $R4 != ""
          ${if} $R4 != "."
          ${andIf} $R4 != ".."
            ${if} ${FileExists} "$INSTDIR\resources\runtime\$R4\.coop-pack"
              DetailPrint "keeping resources\runtime\$R4 for the new version to check"
            ${elseIf} ${FileExists} "$INSTDIR\resources\runtime\$R4\*.*"
              RMDir /r "$INSTDIR\resources\runtime\$R4"
            ${else}
              Delete "$INSTDIR\resources\runtime\$R4"
            ${endIf}
          ${endIf}
          FindNext $R3 $R4
        ${Loop}
        FindClose $R3
      ${elseIf} ${FileExists} "$INSTDIR\resources\$R6\*.*"
        RMDir /r "$INSTDIR\resources\$R6"
      ${else}
        Delete "$INSTDIR\resources\$R6"
      ${endIf}
    ${endIf}
    FindNext $R5 $R6
  ${Loop}
  FindClose $R5
  Pop $R4
  Pop $R3
  Pop $R6
  Pop $R5
!macroend

; The program files' removal (electron-builder inserts this in place of its
; own RMDir /r). An upgrade keeps coop.exe (see the header); the folder's other
; files and folders go one by one. Deleting while FindFirst/FindNext walks the
; folder is fine on NTFS (the handle reads the names as they are).
!macro customRemoveFiles
  SetOutPath $TEMP
  ${if} ${isUpdated}
    DetailPrint "replacing coop's program files (coop.exe stays in place for the taskbar pin until the new one is written)"
    FindFirst $R7 $R8 "$INSTDIR\*"
    ${DoWhile} $R8 != ""
      ${if} $R8 != "."
      ${andIf} $R8 != ".."
      ${andIf} $R8 != "${APP_EXECUTABLE_FILENAME}"
        ; Electron's own files stay too (its DLLs, .pak, .dat, .bin and .json
        ; files and locales\), with resources\app.asar: coop.exe still starts
        ; during the update and shows "coop is updating" (desktop/main.mjs)
        ; instead of a missing-DLL error. The new version overwrites them.
        StrCpy $R1 $R8 "" -4
        StrCpy $R2 $R8 "" -5
        ${if} $R8 == "resources"
          !insertmacro coopRemoveResources
        ${elseIf} $R8 == "locales"
        ${orIf} $R1 == ".dll"
        ${orIf} $R1 == ".pak"
        ${orIf} $R1 == ".dat"
        ${orIf} $R1 == ".bin"
        ${orIf} $R2 == ".json"
          DetailPrint "keeping $R8 until the new version replaces it"
        ${elseIf} ${FileExists} "$INSTDIR\$R8\*.*"
          RMDir /r "$INSTDIR\$R8"
        ${else}
          Delete "$INSTDIR\$R8"
        ${endIf}
      ${endIf}
      FindNext $R7 $R8
    ${Loop}
    FindClose $R7
  ${else}
    RMDir /r $INSTDIR
  ${endIf}
!macroend

!macro customUnInstall
  ${ifNot} ${isUpdated}
    !insertmacro coopPowerShell $R9
    nsExec::ExecToLog '"$R9" -NoLogo -NoProfile -NonInteractive -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File "$INSTDIR\resources\coop\scripts\window-uninstall.ps1" "$INSTDIR"'
    Pop $0
    ${if} $installMode == "all"
      nsExec::ExecToLog '"$R9" -NoLogo -NoProfile -NonInteractive -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File "$INSTDIR\resources\coop\scripts\machine-install.ps1" -Remove -InstallDir "$INSTDIR"'
      Pop $0
    ${endIf}
  ${endIf}
!macroend
